From: ane-stack
Subject: [PATCH 0014] espresso: decode loadModel refusals into typed errors (RUN-1)

`_ANEClient loadModel:options:qos:error:` refusals surfaced as one opaque
string ("loadModel failed: … Program load failure (0x170004)"), so a caller
could only contains() it. examples/dp3.rs did, and its extraction was wrong:
it sliced 8 chars from the first 0x, so a signed code (-0x170004) yielded
"-0x17000" — valid-looking and incorrect.

Adds AneLoadError, carried by a new EspError::Load variant, at the single
place the string was produced:

  code: Option<u32>        parsed leniently (leading '-' accepted)
  kind: AneLoadKind        named variant, or Unrecognised / NoCode
  form: Option<ArtifactForm>  the form the code discriminates
  raw: String              the complete NSError description, unmodified

  suggested_cause() -> Option<&str>   None for unmeasured codes, on purpose
  is_known_deploy_gate() -> bool     true only for the measured three
  presented_form(path)               form inferred from the path

Taxonomy is PROBE-2's measured table, encoded as data:
  0x170004 -> BareMachoRejected / BareMacho
  0x130004 -> EspressoBundleRejected / EspressoBundle
  0x120004 -> E5BundleRejected / E5Bundle

The decode is heuristic over an Apple-private, undocumented string, and is
documented as such: raw is always retained, and an unmeasured code lands on
Unrecognised with no invented cause.

dp3.rs now matches the variant instead of grepping text. Output format stays
compatible, so docs/evidence/0010-deploy-gate-codes.md reproduces as written
(now with kind and form appended). dp3.rs was the only string-grepping caller
in the workspace (searched).

Tests (src/espresso.rs::run1_tests): 9, including a table test over every
measured code, plus guards against guessing an unknown code, the '-0x17000'
bug, malformed tokens, and Display hiding the raw text.

Codes re-verified on hardware after the change, all three families.

